// The legal cells, which any fix must not break. TV accepts all of these and
// so do we. Note the `for` body: a tuple statement there is never a return
// position, which is what kills the "tuple literals are return positions"
// description in INV046 and the tail-tracking machinery built on it.
//@version=6
indicator("legal in-block tuple positions")
a = 1
b = 2

f() =>
    for i = 0 to 1
        [a, b]
        a + b
    [a, b]

g() =>
    switch
        close > open => [a, b]
        => [b, a]

[x, y] = f()
[p, q] = g()
plot(x + y + p + q)
